  [; A read that failed (exit 2) is the ENVIRONMENT, not a label refusal: its
     own sentence, so an unreachable GitHub (no gh, no auth, no network) is
     never read as an issue without its label. ]
  [read-case id=read-gh-not-authenticated repo=cx-private why='`gh api` exited 4: To get started with GitHub CLI, please run:  gh auth login'
    want="issue-label-gate: ENVIRONMENT -- the open issues of cx-private could not be read (`gh api` exited 4: To get started with GitHub CLI, please run:  gh auth login); nothing was judged, this is not a label refusal (exit 2)"]
  [read-case id=read-gh-absent repo=cx-platform-xap why='gh could not be run: no such file'
    want="issue-label-gate: ENVIRONMENT -- the open issues of cx-platform-xap could not be read (gh could not be run: no such file); nothing was judged, this is not a label refusal (exit 2)"]
